    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-120841",
      "knowledge_point_id": "8e53619d-67f3-5992-9280-0f884214eca6",
      "knowledge_point": "Completing the Second Row of a Table Using Euler's Method",
      "problem": "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=x{e}^{-y},\\,y(1)=0\n$$\n\nWe wish to approximate the solution using Euler's method. What entry should be placed in the column for $Δy$ in the second row of the table below if the step size is $Δx=\\frac{1}{2}?$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n| $$ | $$ | $$ | $\\,?\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "To get the values of $x$ and $y$ in the second row, we add $Δx$ to $x$ and $Δy$ to $y,$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx \\\\  & =1+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\  & =0+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these results to our table gives the following:\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n| $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $$ | $$ |\n\nNext, we compute ${y}^{′}$ according to the given rule (using the values of $x$ and $y$ in the second row), and we compute \n$Δy$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =x{e}^{-y} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot {e}^{-1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{e}} \\\\ Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{e}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4\\sqrt{e}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n| $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{e}}$ | $\\frac{3}{4\\sqrt{e}}$ |",
