    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-351669",
      "knowledge_point_id": "8e53619d-67f3-5992-9280-0f884214eca6",
      "knowledge_point": "Completing the Second Row of a Table Using Euler's Method",
      "problem": "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=3\\sqrt{xy},\\,y(4)=1\n$$\n\nWe wish to approximate the solution using Euler's method. What entry should be placed in the column for $Δy$ in the second row of the table below if the step size is $Δx=\\frac{1}{2}?$ Do not round the answer.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $1$ | $6$ | $3$ |\n| $$ | $$ | $$ | {{field-1}} |",
      "worked_solution": "To get the values of $x$ and $y$ in the second row, we add $Δx$ to $x$ and $Δy$ to $y,$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx \\\\  & =4+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\  & =1+3 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these results to our table gives the following:\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $1$ | $6$ | $3$ |\n| $\\frac{9}{2}$ | $4$ | $$ | $$ |\n\nNext, we compute ${y}^{′}$ according to the given rule (using the values of $x$ and $y$ in the second row), and we compute \n$Δy$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =3\\sqrt{xy} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{2}\\cdot 4} \\\\  & =9\\sqrt{2} \\\\ Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =9\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $1$ | $6$ | $3$ |\n| $\\frac{9}{2}$ | $4$ | $9\\sqrt{2}$ | $\\frac{9\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ |",
      "answer_fields": [
